// {1}{G} sorcery: "Target creature you control fights target creature you
// don't control." (Prey Upon's shape, [CR#701.14a].) The fight family's TWO
// same-sort targets are the R2 ambiguity gate's canonical expected firer
// ([[cards-corpus-dry-run]]): an anaphoric read (`It`/`That(Creature)`) of
// either target would be a guess, and `Label` cannot name a TARGET slot
// (labels name effect introductions, not announce-list entries) — so the
// explicit `Target(n)` slots are the fight family's escape hatch, seeded here
// per the calibration ticket and NOT counted as a gate failure. Inherited by
// cards-fidelity-target-sunset: sunsetting `Target(n)` needs a labeling story
// for announce-list slots first.
Normal(
    name: "Sorcery Fight Two Targets",
    mana_cost: [Generic(1), Green],
    types: [Sorcery],
    abilities: [
        Spell(effect: Targeted(
            targets: [
                TargetOne(AllOf([Creature, ControlledBy(Ref(You))])),
                TargetOne(AllOf([Creature, Not(ControlledBy(Ref(You)))])),
            ],
            effect: Fight(Target(0), Target(1)),
        )),
    ],
)
